/*
 * A soul is an object whose existence is dependent on that
 * of its owner, and which can save in one of two ways:
 * by computing an autoload string (as in the old autoload system),
 * or by saving directly as a non-persistent inventory item (as
 * an object).  Though a soul might talk to servers, they do not
 * have independent savefiles, and are not otherwise treated as persistent.
 * Note that from this point of view, the only difference between a
 * soul and an inherited object is their dynamic nature and the
 * mechanism by which they are saved and restored.
 *
 * NOTE: This latter save method is strongly discouraged - it is
 * far preferable to me that souls save only their critical information
 * in their owner (just about every object in the game has heaps of
 * extraneous crap), and, in any case, subobjects which fail to
 * load can crash the game and/or prevent people logging in (whereas
 * we can use call-outs to start souls).  Alternately, it would be
 * nice if wizards would think about and use the `nosave' variable
 * declarator - every object in the game can be saved...
 *
 * Note that all living objects also have a `store', which can be
 * used for a similar purpose.
 */

query_is_soul() {
	return 1;
	}
